{"name":"Dried Caspia","hex":"#b6bf7f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dried","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without water or moisture, said of something that has previously been wet or moist; resulting from the process of drying.","Usually of foods: cured, preserved by drying."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of dry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dried"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caspia","blocks":[{"text":"Caspia is a genus of marine snails, brackish water snails and freshwater snails with a gill and an operculum, an aquatic gastropod mollusk in the family Hydrobiidae. Caspia is the type genus of the Caspiidae, that is a synonym of Pyrgulinae."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caspia","wikidata":"Q5049108"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"dried":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg/En-us-dried.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Illustration Olea europaea0","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Illustration_Olea_europaea0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Olea_europaea0.jpg","ratio":0.6118909991742362,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_Olea_europaea0.jpg","share":0.140625},{"title":"Olea europaea - Köhler–s Medizinal-Pflanzen-229","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Olea_europaea_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-229.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":0.8690036900369004,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olea_europaea_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-229.jpg","share":0.098125},{"title":"Olea europaea 20190506a","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/